10. Add instruction classifications in small increments
======================================================

First exercise: count conditional and unconditional branches separately.
Then add switches, PHIs, returns, calls, invokes, and indirect branches.
Initialize all counters before the loops and print them after traversal.

We first discussed isa<T>(I), from llvm/Support/Casting.h, to ask whether
an instruction has a particular LLVM type. Instruction classes are declared
in llvm/IR/Instructions.h.

The learner preferred switch/case. Use switch (I.getOpcode()) with these
opcode names in this installed LLVM 23 version:

  llvm::Instruction::CondBr     — conditional branch
  llvm::Instruction::UncondBr   — unconditional branch
  llvm::Instruction::Switch    — multiway branch
  llvm::Instruction::PHI       — SSA merge
  llvm::Instruction::Ret       — return
  llvm::Instruction::Call      — call instruction
  llvm::Instruction::Invoke    — call with normal/unwind destinations
  llvm::Instruction::IndirectBr — indirect branch

Increment the appropriate counter and end each case with break. The default
case can do nothing. Increment total_inst before the switch so instructions
such as add and icmp remain part of the total even without their own counters.

Observed correction: an earlier teaching example used Instruction::Br,
which does not exist here. This version has separate CondBr and UncondBr
opcodes. Consult llvm/IR/Instruction.def to inspect the installed names.

Observed bug: a missing break after a branch case would also increment the
switch counter through fallthrough. Compilation success alone would not
detect that counting mistake; the fixture expectations would.

Observed omission: switches was counted but initially absent from the printed
report. Every requested metric must also appear in the output.

These are static instruction counts. One recursive call instruction can
execute many times, but its static call count is still one. Count Call and
Invoke separately. Branch instructions are not the same as successor edges.
Loop counting is deferred to task 1.3 rather than reporting a false zero.


